 "result_text": "`TreeNode.to_dict()` no longer sends the structured metadata fields, so topic nodes should no longer trigger Studio's \"must pass a list of values\" error. I haven't run the tests or tried an upload against Studio.\n\n- **Topic nodes:** I removed `grade_levels`, `resource_types`, `learning_activities`, `accessibility_categories`, `subjects` and `needs` from `TreeNode.to_dict()`.\n- **Content nodes:** I also changed `ContentNode.to_dict()` to include each of those fields only when it's set. Any content node with an unset field would have sent `null` and failed the same way. That part goes beyond the topic-node case in the issue.\n\nThis relies on Studio accepting a missing key. Its check, as the issue describes it, only requires a list when the attribute is included.\n\nBoth changes are in `ricecooker/classes/nodes.py`.",
